    "narrative": "The Austin Waves project a balanced attack today, anchored by the elite tier of **Kyle Tucker** (76.73) and **Andy Pages** (69.49). Both benefit significantly from facing V\u00e1squez, who carries a shaky 4.76 xERA, providing a clear path to high-scoring outcomes. **Jackson Merrill** (67.24) also deserves attention; despite a matchup against the craftier Sasaki, his 13% dynamic platoon boost and the high likelihood of a stolen base attempt against a slow-delivering pitcher make him a priority start. Meanwhile, **Sam Antonacci** (65.19) continues to hold his value at the top of the order, leveraging a 7% platoon advantage and a favorable matchup against Cecconi to secure his status as a locked-in MI option.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the card involved **Nolan Schanuel** (39.91), who fell just shy of our \"Zebras\" floor of 40.0. While **Nolan Schanuel** provided a decent base projection, the harsh 19% penalty associated with Miller\u2019s elite 2.42 xERA pushed him to the bench in favor of higher-ceiling bats. We are also monitoring the risk profile of **Josh Lowe** (43.62); while he barely cleared the bench threshold, he remains a volatile play against Miller, and we are banking on his dynamic platoon advantage to outperform his otherwise suppressive surroundings.\n\nFinally, owners should exercise caution with the bottom half of the order as we navigate a few challenging pitching assignments. **Brayan Rocchio** (41.85) and **Dominic Smith** (48.09) are currently occupying marginal territory; they are starts only because we lack superior alternatives. With **Jordan Westburg** sidelined on the IL, our depth is being tested against these high-efficiency arms. Should any weather or late-scratched lineup news emerge, we will look to pivot to our bench, but for now, the objective is to prioritize the sprint speed opportunities offered by **Jackson Merrill** and the top-order stability of **Drake Baldwin** and **Liam Hicks** to maintain our competitive edge in the stolen base category.",
